\begin_layout Section
3.
 Step-by-Step Initialization Sequence
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To initialize the gSPI (Generic SPI) interface on the CYW43439 for a bare-metal Ada driver you must configure the host microcontroller's SPI peripheral then send a specific sequence of commands to wake up and configure the CYW43439's internal bus interface.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here is the step-by-step process and the exact Ada structures required to complete the initialization.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
Host SPI Configuration (RP2040 Side)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CYW43439 gSPI protocol requires a specific SPI mode and alignment:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
SPI Mode:
 Mode 0 (CPOL = 0,
 CPHA = 0).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Bit Order:
 Most Significant Bit (MSB) first.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Data Width:
 8 bits (transferred in 32-bit words,
 little-endian).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Clock Speed:
 Start low (around 1 MHz to 12 MHz) during initialization.
 
\begin_inset Newline newline
\end_inset

This can e safely increased up to 50 MHz once the chip's internal clocks are fully stable.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsection
2.
 The gSPI Bit Order and Alignment in Ada
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Because ARM Cortex-M0+ and the CYW43439 use little-endian byte ordering you must ensure that your bit-field representation clauses correctly map across the SPI wire.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Here is the exact representation clause for the initialization command:
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
with Interfaces;
 use Interfaces;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
package CYW43439_gSPI is
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
type Function_Block is (Bus_gSPI,
 Backplane,
 WLAN_Data) 
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
with Size => 2;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
for Function_Block use (Bus_gSPI => 0,
 Backplane => 1,
 WLAN_Data => 2);
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
type SPI_Command is record
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Data_Length :
 Unsigned_13;
 -- Bits 0..12
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
