\begin_layout Subsection
3.
 Step-by-Step Initialization Sequence
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To wake up the gSPI bus engine the driver must execute the following hardware sequence:
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Step 1:
 Power-up and Reset (WL_REG_ON)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Physically pull the WL_REG_ON GPIO pin on the microcontroller High to enable the CYW43439's internal regulators.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Assert WL_REG_ON high.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Itemize
Wait at least 50 milliseconds for the internal PMU (Power Management Unit) to stabilize.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Step 2:
 Test the Core gSPI Bus (Read ID)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Before writing configurations confirm that the SPI bus works by reading the gSPI chip ID register located at Function 0 (Bus_gSPI),
 Address 16#0000#.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Construct an SPI_Command with:
 Write_Mode => False,
 Function_Num => Bus_gSPI,
 Address => 0,
 Data_Length => 4.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Assert CS Low.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Transmit the 32-bit command.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Read back a 32-bit status response.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Read back 4 bytes of data.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Assert CS High.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
* Expected Result:
 The upper 16 bits of the data returned should match the default gSPI ID (typically 16#A9A6# or 16#4343# depending on the revision mode).
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
If the upper 16 bits of the data returned are 16#0000# or 16#FFFF# then the physical SPI configuration or wiring is broken.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Step 3:
 Configure gSPI Mode (SPI Word Length)
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
By default,
 the gSPI engine expects 16-bit packet sizes.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To safely use 32-bit standard streaming operations you must write to the gSPI SBSDIO SPIIO Control Register located at Function 0,
 Address 16#012#.
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Register Address Definitions (Function 0)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
gSPI_IO_Ctrl_Reg :
 constant Unsigned_15 := 16#0012#;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Value to write:
 Enable 32-bit word mode,
 high-speed mode,
 and clock setup
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Bit 0:
 Reserved
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Bit 1:
 1 = 32-bit word length mode
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Bit 2:
 1 = High-speed mode
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
gSPI_32Bit_Config :
 constant Unsigned_32 := 16#0000_0006#;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Send a Write command (Write_Mode => True,
 Function_Num => Bus_gSPI,
 Address => gSPI_IO_Ctrl_Reg,
 Data_Length => 4).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Stream out the gSPI_32Bit_Config data word.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Subsubsection
Step 4:
 Request Backplane Clocks
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
The CYW43439 has internal low-power clocks (ILP) and high-throughput backplane clocks (ALP/HT).
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
To access the core Wi-Fi registers request the Active Low Power (ALP) clock via the Clock Control register at Function 0,
 Address 16#001E#.
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
gSPI_Clock_Ctrl_Reg :
 constant Unsigned_15 := 16#001E#;
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
-- Request ALP Clock (Bit 3 = 1)
\end_layout

\begin_layout LyX-Code
Request_ALP_Clock :
 constant Unsigned_32 := 16#0000_0008#;
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Write Request_ALP_Clock to gSPI_Clock_Ctrl_Reg.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Enumerate
Poll this register by performing a Read operation on gSPI_Clock_Ctrl_Reg until Bit 7 (Clock Ready Status) transitions to 1.
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
Once Bit 7 reads back as high the chip's internal backplane is alive and fully initialized.
 
\end_layout

\begin_layout Standard
You can now transition your host microcontroller's SPI clock rate to its maximum speed (up to 50 MHz) and begin accessing Function 1 (Backplane) to load the firmware.
\end_layout

